{
    "summary": "Extends the shop core with store-credit payment and journal, partial and pending/settled refunds settled via provider webhook, and customer returns with a 14-day window, restocking and proportional refunds.",
    "findings": [
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/returns.ts:96-99",
            "finding": "`restockLines` starts its loop at `i = 1`, so the first line of every return is never put back into stock, and a single-line return restocks nothing."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/mail.ts:77",
            "finding": "`sendReturnConfirmation` addresses the mail to `order.id` instead of `order.customer.email`. The id fails the recipient check in `queueMail`, and the resulting error is swallowed by the `catch`, so no return confirmation is ever queued."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:42",
            "finding": "`adminRefund` still limits the amount with `order.total - refundedTotal(order.id)`, but `refundedTotal` now counts only settled refunds. Pending refunds are ignored, so goodwill refunds can exceed what was paid, which breaks the README rule. It also bypasses `requestRefund`, so it should use `refundable(order)` or call `requestRefund`."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/returns.ts:64-66",
            "finding": "`returnAmount` rounds each line's share separately with `Math.round`. The shares of a full return can therefore sum to a cent more or less than `order.total`, so the README promise of paying back exactly what was paid is not guaranteed. An overshoot is rejected by `requestRefund` as exceeding `refundable`. Allocate the remainder to the last return or line instead."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:38-40",
            "finding": "`isRepeat` compares `order.status` with `event.status`, which does not work for `refunded` events. A redelivered event for an already settled refund on a `partially_refunded` order is not recognised as a repeat. `settleRefund` then throws \"already settled\", so the provider keeps retrying. On an order that is already fully `refunded`, any `refunded` event is acknowledged unchecked. Idempotency should be decided on the refund's own status."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "ROBUSTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/credit.ts:48-54",
            "finding": "`spendCredit` reads `balance` before `await book(...)` and writes `balance - amount` afterwards. Two concurrent spends both pass the check and one write overwrites the other, which allows overspending and a lost update. Re-read the balance after the await, or reserve it synchronously."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/report.ts:14",
            "finding": "`revenue` counts only orders with status `paid`. The new `partially_refunded` status drops an order's whole revenue, including the part that was not refunded. The report should count it net of settled refunds."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "ROBUSTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/order.ts:108-109",
            "finding": "If compensating `grantCredit` fails inside the `catch` after `saveOrder` fails, the original error is lost. The customer's credit then stays spent with no order stored, with nothing to reconcile it."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "ROBUSTNESS",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/refund.ts:98-105",
            "finding": "In `issueRefund`, if `settleRefund` throws after a successful `grantCredit`, the credit stays granted while the refund remains `pending`. Only the `grantCredit` failure is rolled back."
        }
    ]
}
```

